  // Decoys (docs/design.md, "Decoys"; the owner 2026-11-02): the Resistance's fakes of the mobile radar, the heavy rocket truck,
  // the tactical missile truck and the cargo truck, built at the vehicle garage (tag vehicle) from its Decoys list (tag decoy).
  // Each only moves: no weapon, ability, set-up, radar, cargo, passengers or driver seat (it drives itself out of the garage
  // and needs nobody to move). disguise names the real archetype it passes for: every player but its owner sees that one (its
  // name, glyph, model, card; HP as a percent; the skirmish AI and every unit choosing targets treat it as the real one:
  // World.ShownArchetype, World.ShownDef). Same locomotor, speed, turn rate, radius, height, crusher and tunnel size as the real
  // one, so neither its look nor its pace gives it away. Flimsy: 60 HP of the real one's armour class (a rifle shot does about 5,
  // a machine gun burst about 4 a round, so small arms take a while; one RPG does 84, a Kornet 69 or more, a mortar bomb 40, a
  // tank shell 250 and any missile or bomb more: one hit kills), no secondary blast (the client deflates it). Not tagged heavy
  // (the strike drone kills it outright) nor radar / air_radar (it emits nothing: the battery links to no decoy and the radar
  // spotting finds none). Vision 2 cells. Cost about a tenth of the real one's, 10 s to build (the cargo truck 5 s).
  // Placeholder numbers: the owner tunes them later.
